1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,563
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:11,916
Ma'am, thank you.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:12,833
Not at all.

4
00:00:13,416 --> 00:00:15,333
Why isn't the pretty girl here?

5
00:00:15,916 --> 00:00:17,166
What do you want?

6
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,833
Be careful. Her boyfriend is right next to you.

7
00:00:20,916 --> 00:00:22,458
That way.

8
00:00:23,791 --> 00:00:26,583
Hey, who exactly are you guys? What do you want from me?

9
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:28,208
What do you know about Yuan Tao?

10
00:00:28,291 --> 00:00:29,666
If Yuan Tao doesn't fall,

11
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,333
my business will stall.

12
00:00:31,416 --> 00:00:35,333
A lot of investors are ditching stocks for that crypto coin.

13
00:00:35,416 --> 00:00:36,666
It's all their fault.

14
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:39,583
Do you know Yuan Tao has a separate company called Tolita?

15
00:00:39,666 --> 00:00:41,041
-Are they related? -Yes.

16
00:00:41,125 --> 00:00:42,791
Tolita is in your line of work.

17
00:00:42,875 --> 00:00:44,250
They run scams.

18
00:00:46,458 --> 00:00:49,958
No wonder they could afford a prime location from day one.

19
00:00:50,041 --> 00:00:52,666
We need your help to scam Tolita.

20
00:00:53,666 --> 00:00:56,791
You'll get a big cut when it's done.

21
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:00,250
So you guys want to scam a peer.

22
00:01:01,166 --> 00:01:03,458
Targeting a peer is tough.

23
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:06,125
I want a deposit.

24
00:01:06,208 --> 00:01:08,250
Send it to me within three days.

25
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:09,500
Money is not an issue.

26
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:13,833
Out with the old, in with the new.

27
00:01:13,916 --> 00:01:18,083
It's a privilege for an old guy like me to learn from the next generation.

28
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:24,000
Don't cheat us.

29
00:01:26,583 --> 00:01:30,333
…an exciting investment opportunity with Dolly Bit.

30
00:01:30,416 --> 00:01:34,333
We all know Bitcoin has grown tremendously since its launch in 2009.

31
00:01:34,416 --> 00:01:39,333
In 2024, it rose above $100,000 for the first time…

32
00:01:57,083 --> 00:01:59,250
THE FIXERS

33
00:02:00,541 --> 00:02:03,916
DIAMOND ICE

34
00:02:06,541 --> 00:02:09,583
A friend who sources seafood

35
00:02:09,666 --> 00:02:11,625
gave me some kind of investment link.

36
00:02:12,333 --> 00:02:15,291
It seemed okay when I looked it up online.

37
00:02:15,375 --> 00:02:19,666
She taught classes on crypto to members.

38
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:22,333
She claimed to be teaching us how to fish.

39
00:02:22,416 --> 00:02:25,375
She invited us into the group and gave us some treats.

40
00:02:25,458 --> 00:02:27,625
Once you got those free coins,

41
00:02:27,708 --> 00:02:31,166
you could invest using their app.

42
00:02:31,875 --> 00:02:34,791
They drove up the price so you thought you were making a profit.

43
00:02:35,541 --> 00:02:36,708
-Four Dots. -Pung.

44
00:02:37,583 --> 00:02:41,583
Later, I discovered she didn't teach us how to fish or give us any fish.

45
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:45,666
She only gave us bait. I was the fish.

46
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:48,000
-Six Dots. -Pung again.

47
00:02:48,083 --> 00:02:50,833
-Are you even listening? -Yeah. Who says I'm not?

48
00:02:51,416 --> 00:02:54,250
Then I found out the app was completely fake.

49
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:56,166
The bullish chart was all a lie.

50
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:58,875
When I told her I wanted to sell, guess what she said?

51
00:02:59,458 --> 00:03:01,791
"Ms. Wu, I'm sorry, our system is down."

52
00:03:01,875 --> 00:03:05,333
Or she would say, "Your account is frozen."

53
00:03:05,416 --> 00:03:09,208
Sounds like every crypto scam company uses pretty much the same tactics.

54
00:03:09,291 --> 00:03:11,000
-Nine Characters. -I won.

55
00:03:11,083 --> 00:03:12,791
Thanks, buddy.

56
00:03:14,916 --> 00:03:16,666
Actually, it's not just me.

57
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:19,625
Several of my customers were also scammed.

58
00:03:20,125 --> 00:03:22,333
-That's not right. -What?

59
00:03:22,416 --> 00:03:24,416
It's not news that you're bad at mah-jongg.

60
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:27,875
He was clearly waiting for either 1, 4, and 7, or 3, 6, and 9.

61
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:29,375
You fed him the win with a 1.

62
00:03:29,458 --> 00:03:30,708
-What's wrong? -Exactly.

63
00:03:30,791 --> 00:03:32,250
What I meant was

64
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:34,083
if the app was fake,

65
00:03:34,166 --> 00:03:35,791
someone would have noticed.

66
00:03:35,875 --> 00:03:38,041
I was listening, okay?

67
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:40,250
You're great at keeping track of the tiles.

68
00:03:40,333 --> 00:03:43,083
At the time, everyone had their eyes on making money.

69
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:45,875
Who would have thought that it was fake?

70
00:03:46,375 --> 00:03:47,541
Just like you.

71
00:03:47,625 --> 00:03:50,916
You were so eager to toss the 9. So what happened to your money?

72
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,125
All gone.

73
00:03:56,291 --> 00:03:57,958
Why did you ask about all this?

74
00:03:59,083 --> 00:04:00,333
It's just…

75
00:04:00,416 --> 00:04:03,000
Our company is conducting anti-fraud training for employees.

76
00:04:03,583 --> 00:04:05,000
That's so nice.

77
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:06,375
Perfect for you.

78
00:04:06,458 --> 00:04:10,250
Gosh, don't embarrass me in front of your boss.

79
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:12,666
Don't be embarrassed. You really need it.

80
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:17,208
Why did you want to see me?

81
00:04:17,958 --> 00:04:21,625
I wanted to know how your search for Gerald is going.

82
00:04:21,708 --> 00:04:23,041
Oh, I see.

83
00:04:23,125 --> 00:04:25,041
I thought I was in trouble.

84
00:04:25,125 --> 00:04:26,791
Well, so, we've discovered

85
00:04:26,875 --> 00:04:30,041
that Yuan Tao cofounder, Zoe, was connected to Gerald.

86
00:04:30,125 --> 00:04:33,708
He disappeared right around the time Zoe died.

87
00:04:34,666 --> 00:04:38,458
We also learned that Zoe and her partner, William, had a falling-out.

88
00:04:38,958 --> 00:04:41,041
We are trying to approach William.

89
00:04:41,125 --> 00:04:43,083
How will you do that?

90
00:04:43,166 --> 00:04:46,458
William set up a company called Tolita, which runs scams.

91
00:04:46,541 --> 00:04:49,625
We want to use this company to find evidence of his fraudulent activities

92
00:04:49,708 --> 00:04:52,791
and force him to tell us more about Zoe.

93
00:04:54,666 --> 00:04:56,875
Well, um, I heard from Fixer Gold

94
00:04:57,541 --> 00:05:00,458
that Gerald is crucial to Ching He's survival.

95
00:05:00,541 --> 00:05:02,708
Is that true?

96
00:05:05,375 --> 00:05:08,750
Two types of people are especially dangerous.

97
00:05:08,833 --> 00:05:12,541
Those who possess crucial evidence.

98
00:05:12,625 --> 00:05:16,541
And those who know too much.

99
00:05:19,125 --> 00:05:20,916
Pretend I didn't ask.

100
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,166
I want to live a little longer.

101
00:05:24,541 --> 00:05:25,541
I'm going now.

102
00:05:27,041 --> 00:05:28,166
Pretend I never asked.

103
00:05:37,166 --> 00:05:38,666
ZOE

104
00:05:43,041 --> 00:05:44,291
Hey, Ben.

105
00:05:44,375 --> 00:05:46,666
Did you open this stall first or the arcade?

106
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:50,000
My dad left me this stall.

107
00:05:50,083 --> 00:05:53,083
I took over right after he passed away.

108
00:05:53,583 --> 00:05:56,625
I bought the arcade after I retired.

109
00:05:56,708 --> 00:05:58,333
What did you do before that?

110
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:02,583
Didn't Mina tell you that I used to be a fixer too?

111
00:06:04,916 --> 00:06:07,250
You were a fixer too? She didn't say.

112
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:09,041
We've barely talked to each other.

113
00:06:09,125 --> 00:06:11,000
Don't you think she's difficult?

114
00:06:11,083 --> 00:06:13,375
Don't you think talking behind people's backs

115
00:06:13,958 --> 00:06:14,958
is really rude?

116
00:06:16,333 --> 00:06:17,208
Your usual?

117
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:23,541
What's her usual?

118
00:06:24,291 --> 00:06:27,875
Tien-bu-la. No radishes or pork meatballs.

119
00:06:27,958 --> 00:06:30,208
What's the point if you don't want those two?

120
00:06:30,291 --> 00:06:32,333
If she doesn't want them, give them to me.

121
00:06:33,791 --> 00:06:35,666
Hey, there you are. Want some?

122
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:36,666
Oh, sure.

123
00:06:37,708 --> 00:06:39,541
-What would you like to eat? -Tien-bu-la.

124
00:06:40,125 --> 00:06:42,250
No blood pudding or deep-fried tofu.

125
00:06:43,375 --> 00:06:45,416
No blood pudding or deep-fried tofu.

126
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:46,625
Goddamn.

127
00:06:46,708 --> 00:06:49,250
Are difficult people all picky eaters?

128
00:06:50,083 --> 00:06:51,958
Young people these days, jeez.

129
00:06:52,041 --> 00:06:54,541
They don't eat this or that. Such a pain in the butt.

130
00:06:54,625 --> 00:06:56,458
Just put both in one bowl.

131
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:58,416
-In one bowl? -Yes, just do as I say.

132
00:07:00,125 --> 00:07:01,333
Here, only one bowl left.

133
00:07:01,916 --> 00:07:03,708
You two will have to make do and share.

134
00:07:04,291 --> 00:07:05,166
Share it.

135
00:07:11,708 --> 00:07:14,250
The app already shows a 15% profit.

136
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:16,458
You move fast. Have you already invested in it?

137
00:07:16,541 --> 00:07:17,583
I bought it.

138
00:07:18,375 --> 00:07:21,875
Ben, contact a crypto broker and convert all the funds.

139
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,000
I installed the app too.

140
00:07:25,083 --> 00:07:28,458
We can see that the price is going up way more slowly for a buyer

141
00:07:28,541 --> 00:07:30,708
than for someone who isn't.

142
00:07:30,791 --> 00:07:31,958
Wait, that's not right.

143
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:36,500
If they want to scam people, the price should surge for buyers.

144
00:07:37,375 --> 00:07:39,000
A slow rise makes you buy more.

145
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:40,541
Otherwise, who would do that?

146
00:07:40,625 --> 00:07:42,375
Everyone would want to cash out.

147
00:07:42,458 --> 00:07:44,458
You see, for an average person like you,

148
00:07:44,541 --> 00:07:46,083
earning less hurts the most.

149
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:47,541
Greedy guts.

150
00:07:47,625 --> 00:07:51,333
Humpty Dumpty sat on a wall, got too greedy, and had a great fall.

151
00:07:51,416 --> 00:07:54,708
Well, this only proves that Tolita runs scams.

152
00:07:54,791 --> 00:07:56,875
There's still no connection to William.

153
00:07:56,958 --> 00:08:00,041
Dolly isn't just a spokesperson or figurehead.

154
00:08:00,125 --> 00:08:03,125
She is essentially running the company.

155
00:08:03,208 --> 00:08:04,666
We need to lure William out.

156
00:08:06,125 --> 00:08:08,250
Then we need an even easier mark.

157
00:08:14,291 --> 00:08:17,333
Don't look at me. I'm five million dollars in debt.

158
00:08:25,083 --> 00:08:26,083
Thirty million.

159
00:08:26,166 --> 00:08:27,416
Holy crap.

160
00:08:27,916 --> 00:08:30,041
HUNG KUO-LUNG'S INVESTMENT PHILOSOPHY, RESUME

161
00:08:32,416 --> 00:08:35,166
Next, we need to make Dolly believe

162
00:08:35,250 --> 00:08:37,958
that you're an easy mark through Hung Kuo-lung.

163
00:08:38,708 --> 00:08:40,125
Mr. Hung, I'm curious.

164
00:08:40,208 --> 00:08:42,791
You are an investment adviser. Why become a broker?

165
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:46,958
Speaking of this makes me sad.

166
00:08:49,291 --> 00:08:52,291
Two weeks ago, my mother passed away.

167
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:54,000
I really…

168
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:56,250
I really can't go on managing client accounts.

169
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:57,291
MEMBER INFORMATION

170
00:08:57,375 --> 00:08:59,916
But I don't want to let them down.

171
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:02,708
How much of a cut do you want?

172
00:09:03,291 --> 00:09:04,208
15%.

173
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:09,083
What you're asking is a first for me.

174
00:09:09,583 --> 00:09:11,375
I need to think about it.

175
00:09:11,458 --> 00:09:12,291
10%?

176
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,250
It's not the percentage. But thank you for the suggestion.

177
00:09:18,666 --> 00:09:22,708
DUBAI, UNITED ARAB EMIRATES

178
00:09:24,416 --> 00:09:27,208
I feel like she sensed something was wrong.

179
00:09:27,291 --> 00:09:30,500
She must think I was lying to her. I could see it in her eyes.

180
00:09:30,583 --> 00:09:33,708
We want her to think you were lying to her.

181
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:36,833
Better yet, she finds out you run investment scams.

182
00:09:36,916 --> 00:09:40,166
Fat sheep selected by a wolf are like goods in a curated store.

183
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:41,208
It's all handpicked.

184
00:09:41,291 --> 00:09:43,333
How could another wolf resist making a move?

185
00:09:45,458 --> 00:09:48,833
You three hustlers found a swindler to cheat a big scammer together.

186
00:09:48,916 --> 00:09:50,125
I'm impressed.

187
00:09:50,208 --> 00:09:51,791
Here, fat sheep. May you get rich.

188
00:09:51,875 --> 00:09:53,083
GREEN DRAGON

189
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,875
I won.

190
00:09:55,541 --> 00:09:58,458
South Wind, Four Seasons, dealer, and single wait. Four points.

191
00:09:58,958 --> 00:10:01,125
Still hoping to win? You're getting fleeced.

192
00:10:01,208 --> 00:10:02,875
You little…

193
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:10,375
Hello?

194
00:10:10,458 --> 00:10:13,041
Hello? Is this Mr. Chiang Ming-shun?

195
00:10:13,125 --> 00:10:14,416
You got the wrong number.

196
00:10:15,541 --> 00:10:17,333
Hey.

197
00:10:17,416 --> 00:10:18,958
Aren't you Mr. Chiang Ming-shun?

198
00:10:19,041 --> 00:10:21,958
I am. Sorry, the signal wasn't great.

199
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,375
Hello, I'm calling from Tolita.

200
00:10:24,458 --> 00:10:25,625
I am the CEO, Dolly.

201
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:26,791
I know.

202
00:10:27,291 --> 00:10:31,333
My investment adviser, Hung Kuo-lung, said he wanted to help me invest in Dolly Bit.

203
00:10:31,416 --> 00:10:34,416
But why did you contact me directly?

204
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:37,833
Well, you're one of our biggest investors.

205
00:10:37,916 --> 00:10:41,208
We would like to invite you to our private investor dinner.

206
00:10:41,291 --> 00:10:42,791
Oh, there's no need.

207
00:10:42,875 --> 00:10:44,291
I'm interested in your product,

208
00:10:44,375 --> 00:10:46,625
but I prefer not to spend time socializing.

209
00:10:46,708 --> 00:10:47,750
How about this?

210
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:50,791
If there's anything, ask your boss to reach out directly.

211
00:10:50,875 --> 00:10:52,250
I'll send you the address.

212
00:10:52,333 --> 00:10:53,208
Um, sorry.

213
00:10:53,291 --> 00:10:54,750
I'm boarding my flight.

214
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,750
-Keep in touch. -Mr. Chiang, let me…

215
00:10:57,583 --> 00:10:58,500
Hello?

216
00:11:02,958 --> 00:11:04,375
Are you flying out?

217
00:11:04,958 --> 00:11:06,791
No.

218
00:11:07,666 --> 00:11:08,833
Did you see a doctor?

219
00:11:08,916 --> 00:11:12,125
My stomach has been bothering me. I keep having diarrhea.

220
00:11:12,208 --> 00:11:15,125
You hate taking medicine. You wouldn't see a doctor for a cold.

221
00:11:15,208 --> 00:11:16,041
What is that for?

222
00:11:16,125 --> 00:11:18,625
The doctor said I must take something for the diarrhea.

223
00:11:18,708 --> 00:11:19,916
Oh, so you won't tell me.

224
00:11:20,416 --> 00:11:21,958
Mom! Mom, Dad--

225
00:11:29,625 --> 00:11:30,583
Okay.

226
00:11:31,750 --> 00:11:32,875
I'll tell you,

227
00:11:33,666 --> 00:11:35,000
but you can't tell your mom.

228
00:11:35,083 --> 00:11:36,000
Okay.

229
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:44,291
Did you see it?

230
00:11:46,333 --> 00:11:47,708
Actually,

231
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:50,750
it keeps shaking.

232
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:52,083
Look.

233
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:54,375
Why is this happening?

234
00:11:54,875 --> 00:11:55,833
Here, not here.

235
00:11:55,916 --> 00:11:57,625
I know. I'm looking over there.

236
00:11:58,625 --> 00:12:00,708
Have you heard of Parkinson's disease?

237
00:12:32,708 --> 00:12:33,833
Sir Hong,

238
00:12:34,583 --> 00:12:37,625
every day, many people come to pray to God.

239
00:12:38,208 --> 00:12:41,875
Just how many people will receive his help?

240
00:12:42,375 --> 00:12:44,083
God helps those who help themselves.

241
00:12:44,583 --> 00:12:45,666
Those who come here

242
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:48,541
believe that holding a stick of incense

243
00:12:48,625 --> 00:12:52,250
and chanting a few words will solve their problems.

244
00:12:54,666 --> 00:12:56,791
You've been at Ching He Temple for many years,

245
00:12:57,291 --> 00:12:58,750
but you don't believe in gods.

246
00:12:58,833 --> 00:13:00,541
That's quite interesting.

247
00:13:02,041 --> 00:13:05,416
I merely don't believe gods would help people like that.

248
00:13:05,916 --> 00:13:08,041
One has to do their best

249
00:13:08,708 --> 00:13:10,791
before letting God do the rest.

250
00:13:14,958 --> 00:13:17,375
Besides Fixer Terra,

251
00:13:18,291 --> 00:13:20,125
who do you think will be on our side?

252
00:13:20,625 --> 00:13:23,208
It doesn't really matter whose side they will be on.

253
00:13:23,708 --> 00:13:24,666
But

254
00:13:25,208 --> 00:13:28,333
if Tristan Hsueh becomes mayor,

255
00:13:28,416 --> 00:13:29,833
that will be a huge problem.

256
00:13:30,916 --> 00:13:33,708
The Hsuehs are a prominent political family.

257
00:13:33,791 --> 00:13:35,833
They have a strong network

258
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:39,000
and financial resources at their disposal.

259
00:13:39,083 --> 00:13:41,625
Their reach even extends into law enforcement.

260
00:13:42,833 --> 00:13:46,166
If Yeh Yueh Tong and the Hsueh family join forces and grow stronger,

261
00:13:47,166 --> 00:13:49,375
you will have to face your fate.

262
00:13:51,708 --> 00:13:55,458
But I still have a pawn that can keep the Hsueh family in check.

263
00:13:56,333 --> 00:13:59,875
A single pawn cannot decide the outcome of the game.

264
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:06,791
Besides, it is uncertain if this pawn will turn out to be black or white.

265
00:14:06,875 --> 00:14:08,750
There was only one pawn,

266
00:14:09,250 --> 00:14:12,666
but God sent another one.

267
00:14:13,625 --> 00:14:15,958
You sent them to find Gerald.

268
00:14:16,458 --> 00:14:17,875
Will that work?

269
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:19,916
I have made every effort.

270
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:23,125
Now it's up to God.

271
00:14:36,791 --> 00:14:37,625
Hey, buddy.

272
00:14:37,708 --> 00:14:40,250
You don't think my reply to Dolly was too harsh?

273
00:14:40,333 --> 00:14:43,875
Hey, it will be bad if she gets upset, and we don't hear back.

274
00:14:43,958 --> 00:14:47,250
You've been around for a while. Haven't you heard of playing hard to get?

275
00:14:47,333 --> 00:14:51,000
That's how I know people will actually walk away if you play too hard to get.

276
00:14:51,083 --> 00:14:54,125
Hey, are you playing hard to get with Mina?

277
00:14:54,208 --> 00:14:56,833
Listen, don't drag this out too long.

278
00:14:56,916 --> 00:14:58,500
-When my wife and I-- -Are you done?

279
00:14:58,583 --> 00:15:01,125
-I am. -Then come out already!

280
00:15:03,583 --> 00:15:04,541
How do I look?

281
00:15:05,375 --> 00:15:06,416
Like a fat sheep?

282
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,333
Like an old man at a wedding banquet.

283
00:15:08,416 --> 00:15:10,125
Why do you insist on this tie?

284
00:15:10,208 --> 00:15:12,666
It looks good. It's the first tie my wife ever gave me.

285
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:13,791
And your hairstyle.

286
00:15:14,291 --> 00:15:16,291
It looks like it's from 50 years ago.

287
00:15:16,375 --> 00:15:18,666
I've had a perm for 50 years. What do you mean?

288
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:19,666
Your belly.

289
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:21,000
It's entirely your issue.

290
00:15:21,875 --> 00:15:23,041
Try another outfit.

291
00:15:23,125 --> 00:15:26,083
Buddy, this is already the tenth.

292
00:15:26,583 --> 00:15:30,083
Never mind, I'll take you somewhere. You'll be satisfied. One sec.

293
00:15:34,041 --> 00:15:35,375
Ya.

294
00:15:36,166 --> 00:15:37,625
Where's Hsien? Is he off today?

295
00:15:37,708 --> 00:15:40,125
Felix! It has been a long time!

296
00:15:40,208 --> 00:15:41,166
Yeah.

297
00:15:41,916 --> 00:15:43,666
Dad passed away over three years ago.

298
00:15:44,333 --> 00:15:45,333
Really?

299
00:15:47,083 --> 00:15:49,583
Your son's suit looks very nice.

300
00:15:49,666 --> 00:15:51,583
-Him? He's too old to be my son. -Yeah.

301
00:15:51,666 --> 00:15:53,416
My son is in junior high right now.

302
00:15:54,041 --> 00:15:57,000
So, Hsien… How did it happen?

303
00:15:57,083 --> 00:16:00,250
He had a sudden stroke and passed away two or three years later.

304
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:01,625
Is that so?

305
00:16:02,125 --> 00:16:03,583
I haven't been here in a decade.

306
00:16:03,666 --> 00:16:06,833
I am Felix's colleague. I'm here to help him pick a suit.

307
00:16:06,916 --> 00:16:08,791
Oh, sure. No problem.

308
00:16:08,875 --> 00:16:10,166
Let's do it.

309
00:16:10,250 --> 00:16:12,416
Felix, where do you work now?

310
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:15,083
I take gigs, I suppose.

311
00:16:17,291 --> 00:16:20,125
182, 96.5, 86.4, 96.5.

312
00:16:21,625 --> 00:16:22,791
He touched me all over.

313
00:16:23,375 --> 00:16:24,875
You were measured eight times.

314
00:16:24,958 --> 00:16:26,708
Time really flies.

315
00:16:26,791 --> 00:16:28,500
I remember when we were younger,

316
00:16:28,583 --> 00:16:30,458
you and Chi would come with liquor.

317
00:16:30,541 --> 00:16:32,125
You guys wouldn't let me drink.

318
00:16:33,125 --> 00:16:34,416
Here, try this.

319
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,458
Who told you to turn Chi down?

320
00:16:37,625 --> 00:16:39,708
A decade went by in a flash. Your dad is gone.

321
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:41,541
Chi is gone too.

322
00:16:48,041 --> 00:16:51,500
That row was made for the crew back then.

323
00:16:51,583 --> 00:16:53,333
That's why it's designed that way.

324
00:16:54,416 --> 00:16:55,958
This one really suits Felix.

325
00:16:56,458 --> 00:16:58,791
He used to hate wearing that style.

326
00:16:58,875 --> 00:17:01,541
He had my dad customize everything for him.

327
00:17:01,625 --> 00:17:03,791
Custom-made is the way to go, okay?

328
00:17:03,875 --> 00:17:06,875
He keeps saying he used to be part of the crew and had great aim.

329
00:17:06,958 --> 00:17:08,500
Many feared him. Is that true?

330
00:17:08,583 --> 00:17:10,333
Felix and Chi were known as

331
00:17:10,416 --> 00:17:12,791
the Black and White Impermanence of the underworld.

332
00:17:12,875 --> 00:17:16,000
One was a stone-faced sharpshooter, the other an intimidating fighter.

333
00:17:16,083 --> 00:17:17,125
Stone-faced?

334
00:17:17,208 --> 00:17:18,625
Yes, he gave himself the name.

335
00:17:18,708 --> 00:17:20,541
Why is he such a smooth talker now?

336
00:17:20,625 --> 00:17:23,833
How else can you survive in the world?

337
00:17:23,916 --> 00:17:24,750
Hey.

338
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:28,625
You two, don't bad-mouth me while I'm changing, okay?

339
00:17:28,708 --> 00:17:31,125
If nothing had happened to Chi back then,

340
00:17:31,208 --> 00:17:33,458
maybe they'd still be prowling the streets.

341
00:17:42,083 --> 00:17:43,041
Hey.

342
00:17:43,125 --> 00:17:44,125
Take a look.

343
00:17:44,625 --> 00:17:45,666
Is it okay?

344
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:48,708
Gosh. So handsome.

345
00:17:49,375 --> 00:17:50,958
-Let me see. -Finally.

346
00:17:51,041 --> 00:17:52,416
Let me check the waistline.

347
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:53,958
No need to alter it. It fits.

348
00:17:54,041 --> 00:17:56,958
-And the pant length? -It's okay. I have a model's build.

349
00:17:57,541 --> 00:17:58,750
You left your clothes.

350
00:17:59,458 --> 00:18:00,708
I don't want them anymore.

351
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:02,541
Good riddance.

352
00:18:03,041 --> 00:18:05,458
THE GENTLEMEN'S SUIT SHOP, PREMIUM SUITS

353
00:18:21,208 --> 00:18:22,250
Mr. Chiang.

354
00:18:23,666 --> 00:18:24,708
Have a seat.

355
00:18:27,458 --> 00:18:28,583
Is he the boss?

356
00:18:29,083 --> 00:18:30,250
He is our crypto broker.

357
00:18:30,333 --> 00:18:31,791
I'm the person in charge, Dolly.

358
00:18:31,875 --> 00:18:34,541
So no one else is above? It's just you?

359
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,458
Yes, I am the person in charge.

360
00:18:40,125 --> 00:18:41,375
You're so young.

361
00:18:41,458 --> 00:18:42,833
Come on, let's eat.

362
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:49,125
Do you find it strange that I chose to meet you here?

363
00:18:49,208 --> 00:18:52,125
Why would we? Who says you need fancy rooms for investment talks?

364
00:18:52,208 --> 00:18:53,125
True.

365
00:18:54,125 --> 00:18:56,750
This stir-fry eatery is where my business started.

366
00:18:57,250 --> 00:18:59,666
Twenty years ago, I sat in this very spot.

367
00:19:00,166 --> 00:19:01,583
I was so poor

368
00:19:02,083 --> 00:19:05,250
that I could only order swamp eel noodles without swamp eel.

369
00:19:07,041 --> 00:19:09,708
Do you know what I overheard the next table talking about?

370
00:19:09,791 --> 00:19:12,250
Venturing abroad.

371
00:19:14,708 --> 00:19:18,625
Hung Kuo-lung runs stock scams. It's best to steer clear of him.

372
00:19:18,708 --> 00:19:23,125
I know. So I went around him and contacted the Taiwanese businessman in Dubai.

373
00:19:23,208 --> 00:19:25,708
Something about his information seems fishy.

374
00:19:26,291 --> 00:19:29,750
Find out what his intentions are. Don't rush into committing. Okay?

375
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,375
Got it.

376
00:19:32,041 --> 00:19:34,875
What about me? When are you going to let me take over Yuan Tao?

377
00:19:35,583 --> 00:19:36,916
It's tiring to keep lying.

378
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,500
I don't trust anyone else with Tolita.

379
00:19:44,375 --> 00:19:45,666
Mr. Chiang, I'm curious.

380
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:48,500
What does your company do in Dubai?

381
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,166
I develop medical technologies.

382
00:19:52,708 --> 00:19:54,166
I did a quick check.

383
00:19:54,250 --> 00:19:57,791
How come I don't see the company generating any cash flow or output?

384
00:20:01,333 --> 00:20:03,625
Listen. The tech company is just a front.

385
00:20:03,708 --> 00:20:07,166
My real business is… in games of chance.

386
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:09,375
Got it?

387
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:11,291
No wonder.

388
00:20:12,166 --> 00:20:13,666
I want to get into investing too.

389
00:20:13,750 --> 00:20:17,791
I don't want others to say that I'm a gambler who relies on luck, yeah?

390
00:20:22,625 --> 00:20:24,000
Excuse me, Mr. Chiang.

391
00:20:24,083 --> 00:20:26,875
We carefully vet each investor at Tolita.

392
00:20:27,458 --> 00:20:31,333
Because, you know, it's fairer and safer for all investors.

393
00:20:35,666 --> 00:20:37,000
You don't believe me?

394
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,333
I'll just be frank.

395
00:20:41,416 --> 00:20:43,458
I know some Taiwanese businessmen in Dubai.

396
00:20:44,041 --> 00:20:47,125
But no one has heard of you.

397
00:20:58,125 --> 00:20:58,958
Take a look.

398
00:21:08,083 --> 00:21:11,625
I know you all like cash, right?

399
00:21:13,916 --> 00:21:15,375
You won't botch it, right?

400
00:21:15,458 --> 00:21:17,500
Mr. Chiang, don't worry.

401
00:21:18,541 --> 00:21:20,291
Okay, come on.

402
00:21:20,375 --> 00:21:23,083
The taste hasn't changed at all in 20 years.

403
00:21:24,458 --> 00:21:28,208
That man couldn't stand my words and took out his money.

404
00:21:28,291 --> 00:21:31,250
That influencer was worried I had no money and tried to bait me.

405
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:33,000
The cash instantly changed her tune.

406
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:36,500
She immediately took it, signed, and showed me the app.

407
00:21:36,583 --> 00:21:39,333
Take care of the cash first. I'll see you later.

408
00:21:39,416 --> 00:21:42,625
She's probably taking the cash directly to a money launderer.

409
00:21:42,708 --> 00:21:44,000
We're following her car.

410
00:21:44,083 --> 00:21:45,416
Okay. Hey.

411
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:47,375
You two wanna come over for a bite after?

412
00:21:47,458 --> 00:21:49,166
I ordered way too much.

413
00:21:49,250 --> 00:21:52,166
If you do come, I'll leave and let you two eat alone, okay?

414
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,875
Why act like strangers? We're so close already, aren't we?

415
00:21:59,958 --> 00:22:01,541
Fine, I'll eat it myself.

416
00:22:13,250 --> 00:22:14,083
Here.

417
00:22:19,916 --> 00:22:22,500
How did you know I only eat these two things?

418
00:22:23,125 --> 00:22:24,125
I didn't.

419
00:22:24,208 --> 00:22:26,250
I just happen to not eat those two.

420
00:22:36,375 --> 00:22:37,916
The money launderer is here.

421
00:22:51,916 --> 00:22:54,333
Why not just buy gold bars on the black market?

422
00:22:54,416 --> 00:22:57,250
The launderer will turn the cash into globally accepted crypto

423
00:22:57,333 --> 00:22:59,375
and transfer it to Dolly's overseas account.

424
00:22:59,458 --> 00:23:03,000
Handling it this way is more discreet.

425
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:06,250
But meeting a launderer doesn't link Tolita to William.

426
00:23:06,333 --> 00:23:08,958
How much have you made according to the app?

427
00:23:09,041 --> 00:23:11,666
Around 4%. Just like you said, it's rising slowly.

428
00:23:11,750 --> 00:23:14,791
Time for another fat sheep to appear with the old one.

429
00:23:16,416 --> 00:23:20,250
My previous investment is showing profits on paper.

430
00:23:20,750 --> 00:23:22,125
I'm not in a hurry to sell.

431
00:23:22,791 --> 00:23:25,083
Let the profits continue to grow.

432
00:23:25,166 --> 00:23:26,375
You're a real big shot.

433
00:23:26,458 --> 00:23:28,666
You know that long-term holding can pay off big.

434
00:23:29,166 --> 00:23:32,541
But why don't you consider adding to your position?

435
00:23:32,625 --> 00:23:34,083
You can rake in more profits.

436
00:23:34,166 --> 00:23:35,625
That's what I thought too.

437
00:23:35,708 --> 00:23:37,958
But I found another investment product.

438
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:41,416
This company helped me earn 40% in less than a month.

439
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:42,791
40%?

440
00:23:43,375 --> 00:23:45,000
How is that possible? Are you sure?

441
00:23:45,083 --> 00:23:48,000
There isn't that much bullish news in the market right now.

442
00:23:48,583 --> 00:23:51,166
Look, this is their invitation.

443
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:55,125
I looked into it. It's a Singaporean company.

444
00:23:55,208 --> 00:23:57,791
But apart from this, there is no other information.

445
00:23:58,375 --> 00:24:00,000
It might be a scam company.

446
00:24:01,458 --> 00:24:02,541
Check it out.

447
00:24:03,041 --> 00:24:06,166
There will be many investors. It's not a bad thing to poach a few.

448
00:24:08,041 --> 00:24:09,625
This is your final task.

449
00:24:09,708 --> 00:24:12,666
Invite your investment clients to our cocktail party.

450
00:24:13,166 --> 00:24:14,166
That's easy.

451
00:24:14,250 --> 00:24:16,291
But will this really lure William out?

452
00:24:16,375 --> 00:24:17,291
Just wait and see.

453
00:24:18,208 --> 00:24:19,750
However, this stack…

454
00:24:32,166 --> 00:24:33,666
Thanks for taking care of me.

455
00:24:33,750 --> 00:24:35,791
Hey, this is the CEO.

456
00:24:35,875 --> 00:24:39,125
She might be young, but she knows finance better than her father.

457
00:24:39,208 --> 00:24:41,458
I'll be counting on you.

458
00:24:41,541 --> 00:24:42,958
Just call me Mandy.

459
00:24:43,041 --> 00:24:44,666
Okay, let's keep in touch.

460
00:24:44,750 --> 00:24:45,833
-Okay. -Sure.

461
00:24:45,916 --> 00:24:46,750
Keep in touch.

462
00:24:46,833 --> 00:24:47,916
Sure, keep in touch.

463
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,666
-See you. -Okay, bye.

464
00:24:50,541 --> 00:24:52,291
Hello, I am the CEO of Tolita.

465
00:24:52,375 --> 00:24:53,416
Call me Dolly.

466
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:55,500
Tolita?

467
00:24:56,041 --> 00:24:56,916
Hello.

468
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:00,083
By the way, that snack you told me about tastes really good.

469
00:25:00,166 --> 00:25:01,458
-Really? -Mandy.

470
00:25:01,541 --> 00:25:02,750
Just wanted to say hello.

471
00:25:02,833 --> 00:25:05,125
The younger son of the Hsuehs, Louis.

472
00:25:05,625 --> 00:25:06,750
-Hello. -Hello.

473
00:25:06,833 --> 00:25:09,083
You're like your brother, a fine fellow.

474
00:25:09,166 --> 00:25:11,708
No, my brother is ambitious. I prefer money.

475
00:25:12,208 --> 00:25:16,166
-How long have you been a member? -Just over a month. I've made a bit.

476
00:25:16,250 --> 00:25:18,458
-There will be many more opportunities. -Of course.

477
00:25:18,541 --> 00:25:21,416
I'll let you chat. I have to go welcome a director.

478
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,458
I'll tell you about some derivatives later.

479
00:25:23,541 --> 00:25:24,750
I'll be waiting for you.

480
00:25:26,625 --> 00:25:27,833
Your suit looks great.

481
00:25:27,916 --> 00:25:29,375
It took me a while to decide.

482
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:39,500
Excuse me. Mind lending me a cigarette?

483
00:25:41,375 --> 00:25:42,291
The pack is done.

484
00:25:45,875 --> 00:25:47,958
You're here to poach clients, aren't you?

485
00:25:49,875 --> 00:25:51,375
Sorry, I don't quite understand.

486
00:25:52,583 --> 00:25:55,625
Trading crypto. I know about your company.

487
00:25:56,208 --> 00:25:57,541
You're quite convincing too.

488
00:25:58,833 --> 00:26:02,208
Every client inside has a nine-figure net worth.

489
00:26:02,958 --> 00:26:04,458
You expect me to hand you a win?

490
00:26:04,541 --> 00:26:08,208
You stole one of my investors, so I came to take a look.

491
00:26:08,708 --> 00:26:09,666
I didn't steal him.

492
00:26:10,250 --> 00:26:12,083
He was drawn in.

493
00:26:14,250 --> 00:26:17,375
For a company this young, you have major clients.

494
00:26:17,458 --> 00:26:19,458
You must have a backer, right?

495
00:26:20,083 --> 00:26:21,583
We are a proper business.

496
00:26:22,083 --> 00:26:23,875
If you want to know,

497
00:26:23,958 --> 00:26:25,625
I'm happy to tell you.

498
00:26:27,958 --> 00:26:30,625
We actually collaborate with Yuan Tao.

499
00:26:30,708 --> 00:26:33,708
Their cofounder, William, is one of our shareholders.

500
00:26:34,708 --> 00:26:37,000
If you join us,

501
00:26:37,083 --> 00:26:38,916
we can share the profits.

502
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:41,166
Of course there will be conditions.

503
00:26:42,666 --> 00:26:44,750
I really thought you were legit.

504
00:26:45,416 --> 00:26:46,458
So you're a scammer.

505
00:26:47,750 --> 00:26:49,041
What makes you say that?

506
00:26:49,541 --> 00:26:51,500
You can't possibly be working with Yuan Tao.

507
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:53,458
Do you know William?

508
00:26:58,125 --> 00:27:01,666
So you are the one who works with Yuan Tao after all.

509
00:27:01,750 --> 00:27:06,333
I was going to say, Tolita has impressive scale for being so young.

510
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:12,541
But doesn't Yuan Tao know Tolita runs financial scams?

511
00:27:13,291 --> 00:27:14,916
Where did you hear these rumors?

512
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:17,083
Don't you know launderers gossip a lot?

513
00:27:17,583 --> 00:27:20,000
But don't worry. I won't run my mouth.

514
00:27:20,083 --> 00:27:22,083
I just want to make money.

515
00:27:23,375 --> 00:27:24,208
How about this?

516
00:27:24,291 --> 00:27:27,333
Since I've attracted these major clients,

517
00:27:27,833 --> 00:27:29,583
why don't we meet with William?

518
00:27:29,666 --> 00:27:32,333
Let's turn a lie into reality and make money together.

519
00:27:36,208 --> 00:27:39,750
If William doesn't know your company runs scams,

520
00:27:40,250 --> 00:27:41,833
I'll keep it a secret for you.

521
00:27:41,916 --> 00:27:45,041
If he knows, I'll do it for both of you.

522
00:27:45,125 --> 00:27:47,916
When I profit from collaborating with Yuan Tao,

523
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,541
I'll give you a cut.

524
00:27:49,625 --> 00:27:50,875
What do you think?

525
00:27:54,791 --> 00:27:56,583
The Hsuehs' younger son was there too?

526
00:27:56,666 --> 00:27:57,625
Yes.

527
00:27:57,708 --> 00:28:00,416
He even said he made a lot of money from investing with that company.

528
00:28:00,916 --> 00:28:04,083
If Mandy knows those launderers, she can't be anyone good.

529
00:28:04,583 --> 00:28:06,583
She can't be scamming Louis, can she?

530
00:28:06,666 --> 00:28:08,333
After all, his family is powerful.

531
00:28:08,833 --> 00:28:11,166
They must be targeting easy marks.

532
00:28:11,250 --> 00:28:14,000
She claims to be collaborating with me.

533
00:28:14,750 --> 00:28:16,250
I can't just leave her be.

534
00:28:18,458 --> 00:28:19,583
So you wanna meet her?

535
00:28:19,666 --> 00:28:21,583
One less enemy can't hurt.

536
00:28:21,666 --> 00:28:23,958
And there are indeed many easy targets.

537
00:28:24,958 --> 00:28:27,041
Okay, let me confirm one thing.

538
00:28:27,125 --> 00:28:29,541
We recommend long-term investments.

539
00:28:29,625 --> 00:28:31,833
We believe in the value of blockchain technology.

540
00:28:31,916 --> 00:28:35,041
It isn't just for short-term speculation.

541
00:28:35,125 --> 00:28:38,250
So, of course, Yuan Tao will continue to focus on this area.

542
00:28:38,333 --> 00:28:40,250
BARRAGE OF BEARISH NEWS TRIGGERS CRYPTO BLOODBATH!

543
00:28:54,333 --> 00:28:56,125
At this age,

544
00:28:56,666 --> 00:28:59,083
I'm no longer used to catching a breeze in the evening

545
00:28:59,583 --> 00:29:00,916
up at a place like this.

546
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:06,333
I only drink tea now.

547
00:29:12,166 --> 00:29:13,875
Long time no see.

548
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:22,250
Pardon the liquor.

549
00:29:27,666 --> 00:29:30,125
My father used to tell me

550
00:29:30,625 --> 00:29:34,041
that of all the branches, he admired you the most.

551
00:29:34,541 --> 00:29:37,500
You are the calmest and shrewdest.

552
00:29:39,875 --> 00:29:42,083
Gosh, let's skip the pleasantries.

553
00:29:42,583 --> 00:29:43,916
What do you want to discuss?

554
00:29:48,666 --> 00:29:52,125
I know you and Thackery are old friends.

555
00:29:52,208 --> 00:29:54,750
That bond is hard to sever.

556
00:29:56,125 --> 00:29:57,833
I just want to remind you

557
00:29:58,333 --> 00:30:00,750
that sometimes, not taking a stance

558
00:30:01,250 --> 00:30:02,958
is a stance in itself.

559
00:30:06,916 --> 00:30:08,125
What if

560
00:30:08,958 --> 00:30:10,666
I choose to take a stance?

561
00:30:14,791 --> 00:30:17,250
All I know is if you don't take a stance,

562
00:30:17,333 --> 00:30:20,458
those rumors will disappear,

563
00:30:21,041 --> 00:30:23,833
and your position will be secure.

564
00:30:23,916 --> 00:30:25,541
And all I know is that

565
00:30:26,125 --> 00:30:30,000
choosing Thackery to take over as Fixer Celestial back then

566
00:30:30,541 --> 00:30:31,750
was the right choice.

567
00:30:31,833 --> 00:30:33,583
But now,

568
00:30:33,666 --> 00:30:37,208
insisting that he stay isn't necessarily a good idea.

569
00:30:39,291 --> 00:30:41,625
Don't forget Ching He's principle.

570
00:30:42,458 --> 00:30:44,375
Turn big problems into small ones

571
00:30:44,458 --> 00:30:46,083
and small problems into nothing.

572
00:31:00,083 --> 00:31:03,666
I'm too old to be out in the wind.

573
00:31:04,250 --> 00:31:08,333
It's a pity I can't enjoy this fine liquor.

574
00:31:13,666 --> 00:31:16,708
I heard you've made quite a bit recently investing with Hsin Yueh.

575
00:31:17,208 --> 00:31:18,541
Aren't you a shareholder?

576
00:31:18,625 --> 00:31:21,791
Mandy told me that only after I invested.

577
00:31:22,625 --> 00:31:24,375
You hid that well.

578
00:31:25,166 --> 00:31:26,791
I really should learn from you.

579
00:31:27,291 --> 00:31:29,625
You already have financial freedom,

580
00:31:30,125 --> 00:31:31,916
but it looks like you're not retiring.

581
00:31:32,416 --> 00:31:34,083
It's like a ball game.

582
00:31:34,166 --> 00:31:35,791
Winning money from someone else

583
00:31:36,291 --> 00:31:37,791
feels like winning a competition.

584
00:31:39,166 --> 00:31:40,833
Most of all, you feel accomplished.

585
00:31:47,416 --> 00:31:49,041
I'm beginning to get it.

586
00:31:53,500 --> 00:31:56,041
Okay. See you at the restaurant.

587
00:31:57,791 --> 00:31:58,625
How was it?

588
00:31:59,125 --> 00:32:00,250
William wants to see me.

589
00:32:01,375 --> 00:32:02,708
Finally.

590
00:32:03,375 --> 00:32:06,500
How will you make him disclose his connection to Tolita?

591
00:32:06,583 --> 00:32:08,500
He now believes I run scams too.

592
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:10,625
If he wants to collaborate,

593
00:32:10,708 --> 00:32:12,375
Tolita will have to come in.

594
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,750
If he doesn't,

595
00:32:15,833 --> 00:32:18,291
he'll ask you not to reveal that Tolita runs scams.

596
00:32:18,375 --> 00:32:21,666
Either way, it will prove that he is connected to the company, right?

597
00:32:26,833 --> 00:32:29,041
It's such a waste for you to be a fixer.

598
00:32:29,125 --> 00:32:31,458
If only I had met you sooner, damn!

599
00:32:32,041 --> 00:32:33,625
My gambling den would've been fine.

600
00:32:34,583 --> 00:32:36,000
You're awesome.

601
00:32:51,833 --> 00:32:54,625
Felix said you're meeting with William tomorrow.

602
00:32:56,500 --> 00:32:57,875
Tomorrow night.

603
00:33:01,250 --> 00:33:02,250
What's on your mind?

604
00:33:04,083 --> 00:33:06,291
I've been investigating all this time.

605
00:33:07,750 --> 00:33:10,416
If the result isn't what I want,

606
00:33:11,041 --> 00:33:12,125
what do I do?

607
00:33:17,083 --> 00:33:18,250
Ben gave you this.

608
00:33:18,333 --> 00:33:20,000
No radishes or pork meatballs.

609
00:33:25,166 --> 00:33:27,000
Do you know he never offers it

610
00:33:27,500 --> 00:33:29,333
unless I order from him?

611
00:33:30,375 --> 00:33:31,875
Just eat.

612
00:33:36,583 --> 00:33:38,166
Why did you want to be a fixer?

613
00:33:44,458 --> 00:33:48,083
If my brother ever runs into a problem he can't handle, I can help.

614
00:33:49,750 --> 00:33:52,291
It'll also remind my dad that he has two sons.

615
00:33:58,625 --> 00:34:00,333
It'll go smoothly tomorrow.

616
00:34:20,541 --> 00:34:21,916
You've improved.

617
00:34:23,166 --> 00:34:24,250
Ten to seven.

618
00:34:24,333 --> 00:34:26,125
Gosh, you're off your game today.

619
00:34:26,208 --> 00:34:29,708
Gotta let you earn a bit sometimes, or I'll have nowhere to play if you move.

620
00:34:29,791 --> 00:34:30,875
Thank you.

621
00:34:30,958 --> 00:34:32,625
-This is for you. -Oh, thank you.

622
00:34:33,125 --> 00:34:34,166
A gun for you.

623
00:34:34,250 --> 00:34:36,375
-Practice more. -I've never gotten this.

624
00:34:36,458 --> 00:34:38,625
-Thank you. Bye. -Come on, I'll treat you.

625
00:34:39,500 --> 00:34:41,916
Haven't been here in a while, and it's up another ten.

626
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:43,625
Prices these days.

627
00:34:46,333 --> 00:34:48,541
What's wrong? Does it not taste good anymore?

628
00:34:49,125 --> 00:34:50,750
Today was your first loss to me.

629
00:34:52,208 --> 00:34:53,875
That's how it's supposed to be.

630
00:34:53,958 --> 00:34:56,375
I will grow old, and you will grow up.

631
00:34:58,000 --> 00:34:59,625
Why won't you tell Mom you're sick?

632
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:03,375
Telling her now will only make her worry more.

633
00:35:03,458 --> 00:35:05,500
I looked it up online.

634
00:35:05,583 --> 00:35:07,875
Do you know your condition will only get worse?

635
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,833
Of course I do.

636
00:35:13,208 --> 00:35:15,625
So one day,

637
00:35:16,125 --> 00:35:18,250
you'll have to take care of your mom, got it?

638
00:35:18,333 --> 00:35:20,958
What are you talking about? Are you underestimating me?

639
00:35:21,041 --> 00:35:22,791
I can take care of you too, okay?

640
00:35:22,875 --> 00:35:25,416
Also, Mom isn't as weak as you make her out to be.

641
00:35:26,458 --> 00:35:27,958
Do I need you to tell me that?

642
00:35:28,041 --> 00:35:30,791
When she's fuming, I can forget about going home.

643
00:35:32,250 --> 00:35:34,875
You'd better start thinking about her birthday gift.

644
00:35:34,958 --> 00:35:36,750
Like I don't know. I've got an idea.

645
00:35:36,833 --> 00:35:39,041
It will definitely satisfy the empress.

646
00:35:41,916 --> 00:35:44,458
Come on, eat. Her favorite stinky tofu shop is closing.

647
00:35:44,958 --> 00:35:46,500
Then hurry up and buy it.

648
00:35:46,583 --> 00:35:48,291
Your chicken cutlet isn't coming that soon.

649
00:35:48,375 --> 00:35:49,208
Good idea.

650
00:35:49,708 --> 00:35:53,375
You can have the teppanyaki noodles, but my chicken cutlet… is off-limits.

651
00:35:53,458 --> 00:35:54,583
Do you hear me?

652
00:35:58,833 --> 00:35:59,666
CHIA-YUN

653
00:35:59,750 --> 00:36:02,833
I've booked the plane ticket. Counting down till I leave.

654
00:36:02,916 --> 00:36:04,500
Don't miss me too much.

655
00:36:18,291 --> 00:36:19,125
Yes.

656
00:36:19,625 --> 00:36:20,666
Yes, okay.

657
00:36:21,750 --> 00:36:23,041
Okay, good.

658
00:36:35,250 --> 00:36:37,416
Fuck, what is this?

659
00:36:54,791 --> 00:36:58,250
It will be handled per party policy. Politics plays no part in this.

660
00:36:58,333 --> 00:37:01,000
We cannot waver in our principles due to political winds,

661
00:37:01,083 --> 00:37:02,833
nor can we let a single incident

662
00:37:02,916 --> 00:37:04,958
dampen our determination for reform.

663
00:37:10,208 --> 00:37:12,250
My father is in good health.

664
00:37:12,333 --> 00:37:15,916
He remains committed to society and its people. Thank you every…

665
00:37:16,458 --> 00:37:18,625
Breaking news…

666
00:37:33,625 --> 00:37:36,000
Don't wait. He's not coming.

667
00:37:37,541 --> 00:37:41,041
From what is known so far, rescue workers found the body in the mountains.

668
00:37:41,125 --> 00:37:43,000
Cause of death and motive remain unclear.

669
00:37:43,083 --> 00:37:46,291
This tragic news shocked more than just the business sector.

670
00:37:46,875 --> 00:37:49,666
Yuan Tao's successor and stock outlook…

671
00:37:49,750 --> 00:37:52,208
YUAN TAO COFOUNDER REPORTEDLY COMMITTED SUICIDE IN THE MOUNTAINS

672
00:41:53,500 --> 00:41:56,291
Subtitle translation by: Hannah Liu
